  11. Notable Observations (raw, no fixes)

  1. Bundle budget is tight. Pipeline chunk at 98.8% of its 135 KB limit. Total JS at 98.5% of 1110 KB limit. One new dependency or feature expansion could break the build.
  2. SubscriptionContext is browser-local only. hasServerBackedEntitlement: false is hardcoded. The "paid" gate is just a localStorage flag — no server validation.
  3. No TypeScript. Entire codebase is JSX/JS with no tsconfig. Type checking relies purely on eslint.
  4. Wave 1 pipeline features all disabled. LOD tiers, keyboard shortcuts, web worker layout, collapsible groups, etc. — all false. Wave 2-5 all true. This means the pipeline has advanced
  features (slicing, compositions, experiments) but lacks basic usability features (keyboard nav, LOD rendering, group collapse).
  5. No .env files. API URL is runtime-configured. The vite dev proxy targets localhost:8002.
  6. MSW mocking is comprehensive — session flow, analytics, traces all have authored fixtures. Generated handlers from OpenAPI complement these.
  7. The useSession and useConnectionStatus hooks are thin re-exports of their context hooks — indirection layer that may or may not be intentional.
  8. All 20 pages are lazy-loaded with instrumented timing via lazyPage() wrapper.
  9. requestClient.js auto-unwraps { data, meta } envelope and attaches meta as non-enumerable __meta property on the data object.
  10. Pipeline.jsx at 23,921 bytes is the largest page file by far. Second is StrategyDashboard.jsx at 18,464 bytes.